{"content":[{"c":["JOIADA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Paseah’s son who, with Meshullam, repaired the Old Gate in the Jerusalem wall during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.6","r":"Neh.3.6","rawR":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.6","value":"Neh.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levite and high priest in Jerusalem during the postexilic era, the great-grandson of Jeshua, son of Eliashib, and father of Jonathan (“Johanan” or “Jehohanan,” ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.10-11,22","r":"Neh.12.10-11,22","rawR":"Neh.12.10-11,22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.10-11,22","value":"Neh.12.10-11,22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:10-11, 22"},"). He is alternately called Jehoiada in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.28","r":"Neh.13.28","rawR":"Neh.13.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.28","value":"Neh.13.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 13:28"},", where we read that one of his sons was expelled from the priesthood for marrying a daughter of Sanballat, governor of Samaria."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Joiada","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.6"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:10-11, 22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.10-11,22","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.10-11,22","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.10-11,22"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 13:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.28","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.28","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c4fd4be67ec13c006823671aadda4b7f044c914c88045788f139628ab7c4675a","sourceItemName":"Joiada","sourceItemOrder":288,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Joiada","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Joiada","title":"Joiada","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}